<section class="band band--off">
  <div class="wrap prose">
    <p>I compose music. The soundtracks for my favourite books and stories.</p>
    <p>I grew up reading sci-fi and magic realism 📚, watching Cosmos and the Ascent of Man💡, listening to Vangelis, Jean-Michel Jarre, Tangerine Dream, Orbital, Mike Oldfield, Deep Forest, Astral Projection, Bach, Mozart, Saint-Saëns, Williams, Lito Vitale, Astor Piazzolla, and more recently Trentemoller, Tycho, Air, Newton Howard, Zimmer, Göransson... 🎹</p>
    <p>In 1988, my dad got me a Kawai K5m additive digital multidimensional synthesizer. I got a midi keyboard and hooked it to my PC, used Mastertracks as sequencer, and started blurting out ideas. The initial experiments had low signal to noise ratio, but I never stopped working, learning, enjoying the creative process.</p>
    <p>Today, my music is inspired and suggestive in style of my numerous influences, a maelstrom of ideas about humanity's collective passion to explore and discover new worlds, expand our presence outside Earth 🚀.</p>
    <p>To expand the light of consciousness.</p>
  </div>
</section>

